/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:2: 
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:3: Published 2026-10-18 UTC (2026-10-17 in Los Angeles). The rental GPUs have been
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:4: returned. **C remains uncollected and unscored; MPC has not been evaluated.**
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:5: 
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:6: ## What changed and why
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:7: 
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:8: The original per-request HTTP-client excitation A stopped at 210 s: the scheduled
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:9: 96→48 budget application lag was 52.884 ms against the 50 ms limit. The command
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:10: was applied, but the run correctly aborted and remains invalid for a whole-run
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:11: comparison. A 39.960 ms HTTP client construction overlapped that dispatch-to-
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:12: application interval; no gateway GC overlapped it. These are elapsed spans,
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:13: not exclusive CPU attribution.
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:14: 
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:15: The opt-in `--shared-upstream-client` mode creates one transport at gateway
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:16: startup, keeps request response/reservation cleanup independent, prevents
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:17: response-cookie carryover, and closes the transport at shutdown. It preserves
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:18: legacy mode and the original gates. Runtime `d0ccb2c` passed the complete native
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:19: Linux CPU/mock suite on two rental hosts: 476 cases on each, no failures/errors/
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:20: skips. That evidence is for the collection runtime, not an assertion that a
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:21: documentation-only publication commit was separately run on a rental GPU.
/home/daniel_lin/gt/pr32/mayor/mpc-local-r21/results/shared-client-20261018/report.md:22: 
